{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793641942,"nonce":"QDEKsNq5rzbV2pVap2dVqeQdKOI=","title":"string.byte, select, tonumber, table.unpack build boxed multi-return lists","message":"string.byte is declared Ret::Multi (library/stdlib.rs) and always builds a List\u003cAny\u003e, boxes each byte and wraps the list in a boxed tuple, even for s:byte(i). There is no single-result path to zl_byte_at. tonumber, select and table.unpack/pack share the shape.\n\nRepro: for i=1,#s do if s:byte(i)==101 then c=c+1 end end over 1,000,000 bytes: 46 ms zylua, 1.1 ms LuaJIT, 32 ms Lua 5.5. select('#', ...) x500k: 64 ms vs 19 ms Lua 5.5. tonumber('123') x300k: 26 ms vs 7.6 ms.\n\nDirection: lower calls whose result count is known at the call site (one value) to the scalar form; keep Multi for the open-ended case.","files":null}]}